              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्राकारः — prākāraḥ — \"a town wall; a rampart\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नगरं परितः उन्नतः प्राकारः अस्ति। nagaraṃ paritaḥ unnataḥ prākāraḥ asti. Around the city there is a high rampart."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्राकारः (prākāraḥ) is built from prā, a form of pra, and the root √kṝ, \"to pour out, to heap\"; MW gives prākāra as a wall or enclosure, a rampart (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
